// MulThree -- the Pyrope equivalent of verilog/MulThree.sv (DatapathBench).
//
// Hand-written, not emitted from the Verilog: a machine emission would enter
// the same LGraph the Verilog does and measure the two FRONT ENDS rather than
// the two languages. See [status].pyrope in design.toml.
//
// Ports keep the Verilog names and the widths of the pinned point (BW = 32),
// so the generated harness and LEC bind the same external interface.
//
// Triple product in the 32-bit operand width. Each partial product is
// truncated as it is formed, which is what the Verilog's 32-bit context does
// (the same value as truncating once, and far cheaper to prove). `d` is
// declared but unused upstream; it stays in the interface so both sides bind
// the same ports.
pub comb MulThree(a:u32, b:u32, c:u32, d:u32) -> (product:u32) {
  wrap const ab:u32 = a*b
  wrap product = ab*c
}
